From b7259fbab404a9f9ef224bdc1cd1a3c37a14ed81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Han <danielhanchen@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 09:24:25 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Block swap: lossless compressed weight fetch for bf16 layers
 (opt in)

UNSLOTH_BLOCK_SWAP_COMPRESS=1 stores each swapped bf16 layer's host copy with a fixed width codec
(sign + mantissa byte, 4 bit index into a per 64K word table of the 15 most common exponents, escapes
patched exactly) and decodes it on the card on a side stream, overlapped with the next chunk's copy.
About 25% fewer bytes over PCIe per fetch, bit exact weights, host copies shrink by the same amount.
